From 91cf01549a89b1ca74cc58526a55913a9368a19b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:40:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] types: 64-bit integers 4-byte aligned, as on the DS
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

MWCC lays out u64/s64 inside structs with 4-byte alignment (the old ARM ABI).
GCC's ARM EABI, and GCC with -malign-double, align them to 8, which moves the
fields after one and pads every struct that holds one.

Measured with tools/layout_probe (the same 702 sizeof/offsetof values, compiled
by MWCC 2.0/sp2p2 under Wine and by GCC) on the save-chunk root types of the
pinned decomp: GCC -m32 with 4-byte u64 matches MWCC in all 702 values; devkitARM
GCC and GCC -m32 -malign-double differ in 55, in POKEWALKER (irClock 252 vs 256,
linkCount, steps, watts, unlockedCourses), PCStorage (74492 vs 74496) and
BattleRecord (7504 vs 7512; header, data). Those structs are in the save, so the
unpatched build would read and write a different save layout.

u64 and s64 are declared aligned(4) under SDK_PORT_3DS, as in
pokeplatinum-3ds NitroSDK 0016. The DS build never defines SDK_PORT_3DS, so its
text is unchanged. lib/include/nitro/types.h is the only definition site in
lib/include; vu64/vs64/REGType64 are typedefs of these and follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/include/nitro/types.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/include/nitro/types.h b/lib/include/nitro/types.h
index a821147..5e7136b 100644
--- a/lib/include/nitro/types.h
+++ b/lib/include/nitro/types.h
@@ -10,8 +10,17 @@ typedef signed char s8;
 typedef signed short int s16;
 typedef signed long s32;
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// 4-byte aligned, as the DS's compiler laid them out (the old ARM ABI, with MWCC). GCC's ARM EABI and
+// -malign-double align 64-bit integers to 8, which moves the fields after one and pads every struct that
+// holds one; for the save data that changes sizes and offsets (POKEWALKER, PCStorage, BattleRecord;
+// tools/layout_probe). A smaller alignment on a typedef is what GCC allows for this.
+typedef unsigned long long int u64 __attribute__((aligned(4)));
+typedef signed long long int s64 __attribute__((aligned(4)));
+#else
 typedef unsigned long long int u64;
 typedef signed long long int s64;
+#endif
 
 typedef volatile u8 vu8;
 typedef volatile u16 vu16;
